    "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt transforms the traditional cultural-criticism dichotomy of nature and artifice in The Human Condition by subordinating ecological concerns to political philosophy, arguing that modernity's primary threat is the re-naturalization and triumph of biological necessity over human liberty and plurality."
